<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    GENERATED SHAPE, HAND-KEPT FILE. The expanded panel as native views
    (CCBG-26 (Panel Scaling)) — the single layout's full form.
    Its twin, notif_panel_duet.xml, has the same view ids and
    differs only in static dp: PinnedNotification.fillPanel fills either without knowing
    which it has.

    Why native views and not the old bitmap: RemoteViews never learns the card's width
    or the height Android leaves under the header blocks, so a bitmap taller than that
    room was scaled down uniformly by its ImageView — strips and Weekly rows shrinking
    together to ~60%. A TextView is exactly as tall as its sp says and as wide as the
    card, and the bar ImageViews stretch a nominal-width bitmap with fitXY, which is
    what the header bars already do. Nothing here can be scaled.

    Slots: three strips, one overflow line, four bar rows. What is shown is decided in
    Kotlin; unused slots are GONE. Strips carry title and a two-line detail; the overflow line is its own row, as before.

    Text colours come from the platform's notification appearances, never from
    ?android:attr/textColorPrimary (see notif_duet_expanded.xml).
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
